{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/the-world-below/1533781-sell-me-on-at-the-gates","id":1533781,"title":"Sell me on At the Gates","path":["Home","Onyx Path","Onyx Path Worlds","The Earthbane Cycle","The World Below"],"posts":[{"date":"2024-04-07T19:02:26-07:00","id":1533781,"title":"Sell me on At the Gates","content":"So we are few weeks till the crowdfunding of <b>At the Gates</b> game. ( <b>AtG</b> for short from now. ) We got some previews <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/category/worlds/earthbane/at-the-gates/\" target=\"_blank\">blog posts about it</a> and some tease here and there on Pathcasts. So let's see if we can sell me this game...<br /> <br /> (Correct me if I'm wrong) <b>At the Gates</b> is jRPG-like setting. We talk here about things like <b>Final Fantasy </b>(<b> FF </b>for short ) , and more like 8 and 9, than 7 - those first two were much more traditional fantasy and 7 was much more urban fantasy. So how does this compare to <b>Fabula Ultima</b>, other jRPG great system from last year? ( We literally have now in Poland crowdfunding for translation <b>Fabula</b>, right now. )<br /> <br /> In <b>AtG</b> we have world of Gaia, where 'world is returning from magical apocalypse' ( World Below? ), briming with magic. Even peasants have spells right now. There is something called <b>the Void</b> ( analog to <b>MtAw</b> or <b>Exalted</b> Abyss? ), we have Deamons ( I assume they are like <b>FF</b> Summons ), we have <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/at-the-gates-creatures-of-gaia/\" target=\"_blank\">Elemental Dragons and Elemental beings</a>. We also have Bat and Bear-People in previews.<br /> <br /> Something I missed?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":25411,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25411-travislegge","user":"TravisLegge","date":".  Edited to remove external links. 04-07-2024, 11:09 PM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T00:21:47-07:00","id":1533877,"title":"","content":"Danielle in <a href=\"https://theonyxpath.com/argh-my-eyes-monday-meeting-notes/\" target=\"_blank\">this week Monday Meeting Notes</a> is writing on design concepts of AtG and how she implemented them:<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Monday Meeting Notes</strong> </div> <div class=\"message\"><b>At the Gates</b><br /> <br /> Since the ashcan came out, and we\u2019re getting ready to crowdfund this hopefully soon, I wanted to chat a little bit about what <b>At the Gates</b> is, what it isn\u2019t, and why it exists.When I first started working on Storypath, before I ever did the update, I thought the system would work really well for a high-fantasy spell-slinging game. I spent some time coming up with an idea for what kind of fantasy game <i>I\u2019d</i> like to see and play, and it involved people who are diverse, but diversity isn\u2019t gamified. A setting that had a variety of play styles for fantasy, but focused on being heroic. A game that had clear goals, hooks, and made it clear from the beginning what it is you\u2019re supposed to be doing in it. So, I set to work creating this kind of setting. I am a huge fan of political intrigue, hard choices, moral ambiguity, and exploring the other through a lense of curiosity and compassion. So, of course, I put all that into my setting. As I was writing things up, I realized how much games like <i>Final Fantasy 9, Chrono Trigger, The Secret of Mana,</i> and others were influencing what I was writing. The further I got into the concept, the more I realized I had pretty much written the setting of a JRPG that didn\u2019t exist. When I pitched the game to Rich (back in 2019, in the before-times) it wasn\u2019t originally conceptually a jrpg, but he suggested that we just lean into it. So I did.<br /> I tweaked a few things here and there, but honestly, it was already there. Then when we started working on SP Ultra, I knew that this game was going to be very suited to its style. I was able to add in the concept of magical attacks, teamwork stunts that you can purchase with your bond Enhancement, and a slew of other really fun things that harken to playing a JRPG. If you\u2019re knowledgeable about those games, you\u2019ll see little bits here and there that remind you of many different games. If you aren\u2019t familiar with JRPGs at all, that\u2019s okay. I crafted the world to be rich and full of fun concepts that anyone can enjoy, you aren\u2019t missing anything by not noticing the inspirations, because we didn\u2019t decide to make the game referential.<br /> <br /> If you like fantasy games where the heroes are competent, it encourages you to explore, make hard choices, engage in political issues, fight against evil, and be big heroes, then I think you\u2019ll enjoy <b>At the Gates. </b><br /> <br /> Danielle</div> </div> </div> </div>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":1437,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","user":"wyrdhamster","date":". 04-09-2024, 03:25 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1437-wyrdhamster","name":"wyrdhamster","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1437_5.jpg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11313"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2024-04-09T17:35:06-07:00","id":1533914,"title":"","content":"It has been quite some time since I have been as eager to read more about a game and get involved with playing something. Because of the day job, I sometimes go for periods of being out of the loop, concerning OPP and other gaming. But then I caught a reference to AtG in the most recent Monday Notes. Storypath + Fantasy? Full stop. I am in. With more interest than I have in....pretty much any other RPG I can think of. Enough for me to go back and check out TWB too.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/26185-sebastianf","name":"SebastianF","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2020"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}